.TH PAPERWEIGHT\-KEYS 1 "2026-11-08" "paperweight-skel 0.2.87" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
paperweight\-keys \- show the sway keybindings currently in effect
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B paperweight\-keys
.RB [ \-p | \-\-print ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B paperweight\-keys
reads your sway configuration and lists its keybindings with a short
description of each, in a searchable
.BR wofi (1)
window.
Typing filters the list; Enter or Esc closes it.
It is also the
.B Keybindings
entry in the
.BR paperweight\-settings (1)
menu.
.PP
The files read are the ones sway includes, in the same order:
.I ~/.config/sway/config
followed by
.IR ~/.config/sway/config.d/*.conf .
When two bindings use the same keys, the later one wins, as in sway.
Bindings inside a
.B mode
block (such as the resize mode) are not listed, since they only apply
inside that mode.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-print
Print the list to standard output instead of opening wofi.
This is also the behaviour when no Wayland session is detected.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short usage summary.
.SH LABELS
Descriptions come from comments that start with
.B #:
in the sway config:
.TP
.B #: Description
labels the next
.B bindsym
below it (other comments in between are fine; a blank line ends it).
.TP
.B #: Keys | Description
adds one row for a group of bindings, such as
.BR "#: Super+0-9 | Switch to workspace" .
.PP
A binding with no label of its own borrows the label of the identical
line in the matching file under
.IR /etc/skel/.config/sway/ ,
so a config copied from an older PaperweightOS version is still labeled.
Unlabeled lines that match
.I /etc/skel
exactly are hidden; these are the per\-key lines a group row already covers.
A binding you added yourself, or a stock line you changed, is listed with
its command as the description unless you give it a
.B #:
label.
.PP
Key names are shown in a friendlier form:
.B $mod
(Mod4) as Super, Mod1 as Alt, Return as Enter, comma as \(lq,\(rq, and so on.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sway/config
.TQ
.I ~/.config/sway/config.d/*.conf
Your sway configuration, read on every run.
.TP
.I /etc/skel/.config/sway/
Stock configuration shipped by the PaperweightOS packages; source of
borrowed labels.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR paperweight\-settings (1),
.BR sway (5),
.BR wofi (1)
